From: OpenHarmony PC Adaptation <noreply@openharmony.io>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:01:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] cmake: build UserInterface independently of tests

The cling driver always links clingUserInterface, including static builds.
Defining that runtime library only when CLING_INCLUDE_TESTS is enabled leaves
the driver link item unresolved when tests are disabled. CMake then treats the
plain item as an external library name and emits -lclingUserInterface.

Build the runtime component unconditionally while keeping the test suite
disabled by CLING_INCLUDE_TESTS.

Origin: https://github.com/root-project/cling/tree/v1.3
Upstream-Status: Not-Submitted [contest adaptation]
Source-Commit: af630d98a4aff3868de049d528402a628da0830a
Modification-Layer: 1 (CMakeLists.txt source)
Knowledge-Ref: E215
---
 lib/CMakeLists.txt | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/CMakeLists.txt b/lib/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/lib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/lib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -9,6 +9,5 @@
 add_subdirectory(Interpreter)
 add_subdirectory(MetaProcessor)
-if(CLING_INCLUDE_TESTS)
-   add_subdirectory(UserInterface)
-endif()
+# The driver always links this runtime component, independently of tests.
+add_subdirectory(UserInterface)
 add_subdirectory(Utils)
--
